Use the first guide's composition: mast tip about28percent from top, base feet about71percent; full tower axis roughly43percent of canvas height. Broad park margins around the tower. Do not make a giant tower touching the image borders. Keep foliage outside the complete tower exterior silhouette, no foreground trees hiding the body or foot hall. Natural asymmetrical park planting and gravel paths viewed from above; only tower and cream base hall are architectural subjects.\n\nUse corrected physical dimensions from Task253: steel body ends58.7m, lower octagonal observation gallery FLOOR20m, upper glazed gallery FLOOR51m, slender antenna mast about12m more to around71m total (estimated). Do not use old60/55m heights or move the physical lower gallery to halfway up the body. With this high downward perspective, lower floor appears near62percent from top, upper floor around43percent, body roof around38percent; these are projection hints rather than changes in meters. Real Petřín1891 octagonal/eight-sided riveted steel structure, multiple slender splayed perimeter supports, thin central octagonal core and twin spiral stairs. Not a square/four-legged Eiffel tower. Pale cool blue-gray steel, delicate lattice lower balcony with a small glazed ring above, octagonal glazed upper lantern with shallow gray roof and slim antenna. Cream octagonal hall roughly22m wide, gray shallow roof with real metal seams and subtle weathering; do not invent a large modern roof complex. Low hall facets and restrained windows/arches visible, entrance if visible only obliquely with blank red panels. No extra gallery platforms, copied main entrance front view, restaurant annex, terrace, umbrella, vehicles, satellite dishes or advertising.\n\nBelievable ordinary high-quality real-camera photograph, natural green spring/summer trees with irregular varied crowns, real grass/gravel, matte metal rivets, plaster and glass, gentle daylight and coherent shadows. No CGI/plastic lattice, painting, watercolor, diagram, repeating foliage pattern, miniature-model look, tilt-shift, HDR oversharpening or cinematic night/sunset. Brand-new neutral park background, NO recognizable Prague old-town buildings, statues, protected artworks, walls, museums, ads or brands. No people or vehicles. Only exact small legible Finnish label 'havainnekuva' in lower corner; no other text/logos. Largest native3:2 LANDSCAPE image available, preferably2400x1600; no upscale. One image only.",
